    "rationale": "ABCA3 localizes to lamellar bodies in alveolar type II cells and transports phospholipids needed for normal surfactant assembly. Biallelic loss-of-function variants therefore impair lamellar-body surfactant lipid packaging and can cause severe respiratory disease in term newborns. Strongest alternative resolved: Other surfactant abnormalities can cause neonatal respiratory failure, but biallelic ABCA3 loss plus abnormal lamellar bodies specifically identifies defective phospholipid transport/packaging into lamellar bodies."
